# The gate fixtures use BARE placeholder module specifiers:
#
#     import { fileCardActionFor } from __ACTIONS__;
#
# They are substituted with real absolute paths at BUILD time by the
# gate (the placeholder is replaced with `JSON.stringify(path)`, which
# already carries its own quotes). A quoted placeholder would double
# them.
#
# ★ They cannot be parsed, so prettier cannot format them. ★ They are
# not valid modules — they are TEMPLATES, and a template that a
# formatter cannot read is exactly the kind of file that must be
# excluded from the formatter rather than rewritten to satisfy it.
#
# The R376 format gate runs `prettier --check` over
# `scripts/**/*.{ts,tsx,mjs,js}`, so without this the format gate
# would fail on a file that is SUPPOSED to be unparseable.
